00:23:32,307 --> 00:23:38,307
Tarlov cysts, also known as perineural cysts, are cerebrospinal fluid (CSF)-filled lesions that most commonly develop in the
sacral region of the spinal canal (S1–S5), and less frequently in the cervical, thoracic, or lumbar spine.

10
00:26:09,230 --> 00:26:15,230
These cysts form as dilations of the nerve root sheath near the dorsal root ganglion,
specifically within the perineural space between the endoneurium and perineurium.

11
00:28:46,153 --> 00:28:52,153
A defining feature is that the cyst walls contain nerve fibers,
which often line the inner cavity of the cyst itself.

12
00:31:23,076 --> 00:31:29,076
This involvement of neural elements distinguishes Tarlov cysts from other extradural
meningeal cysts, such as meningeal diverticula, which do not contain nerve fibers.

13
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
The etiology of these cysts is not well understood; some current theories explaining this phenomenon include increased spinal fluid
pressure, filling of congenital cysts with one-way valves, and/or inflammation in response to trauma and disease.

14
00:36:36,923 --> 00:36:42,923
They are named after an American neurosurgeon Isadore
Tarlov, who described them in 1938.

15
00:39:13,846 --> 00:39:19,846
These cysts are often detected incidentally during MRI or
CT scans for other medical conditions.

16
00:41:50,769 --> 00:41:56,769
They are also observed using magnetic resonance neurography with
communicating subarachnoid cysts of the spinal meninges.

17
00:44:27,692 --> 00:44:33,692
Cysts with diameters of 1cm or larger are more likely to be symptomatic; although
cysts of any size may be symptomatic dependent on location and etiology.

18
00:47:04,615 --> 00:47:10,615
Some 40% of patients with symptomatic Tarlov cysts can
associate a history of trauma or childbirth.

19
00:49:41,538 --> 00:49:47,538
Current treatment options include CSF aspiration, Aspiration and Fibrin Glue Injection (AFGI),
laminectomy with wrapping of the cyst, among other surgical treatment approaches.

20
00:52:18,461 --> 00:52:24,461
Interventional treatment of Tarlov cysts is the only means by which symptoms might
permanently be resolved due to the fact that the cysts often refill after aspiration.

21
00:54:55,384 --> 00:55:01,384
Tarlov cysts often enlarge over time, especially if
the sac has a check valve type opening.

22
00:57:32,307 --> 00:57:38,307
They are differentiated from other meningeal and arachnoid cysts because they are innervated
and diagnosis can in cases be demonstrated with subarachnoid communication.

23
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:15,230
Tarlov perineural cysts have occasionally been observed in patients with connective tissue
disorders such as Marfan syndrome, Ehlers–Danlos syndrome, and Loeys–Dietz syndrome.

24
